description:
We are looking for a passionate AI/ML Developer expert in Python and Algorithms. We want to develop AI/ML solution for our product to analyze past logs of user's activity and make a decision based on that analysis.

Responsibilities:

- Design and develop machine learning algorithms;
- Discover, design, and develop analytical methods to support novel approaches of data and information processing;
- Design and develop novel algorithms;
- Perform exploratory data analyses;
- Generate and test working hypotheses;
- Prepare and analyze historical data and identify patterns;
- Provide technical support for program management and business development activities including proposal writing and customer development;
- Own and manage knowledge sharing within a community.

Your profile:

- Artificial Intelligence /Machine Learning experience using Python Programming Language;
- Experience in Predictive Analysis and Algorithms
- Good to have experience in Adaptive Authentication/Risk-based authentication;
- Graduated in Computer Science or similar relevant field;
- Excellent project and time management skills;
- Attention to details;
- Outstanding problem solving and analytical skills.

We are seeking a WordPress Support Specialist to join our team. The ideal candidate will have a deep understanding of the platform and be able to provide technical support to clients using WordPress websites and applications. You will be responsible for troubleshooting and resolving technical issues, as well as assisting clients with any questions or concerns they may have.

Responsibilities

Troubleshoot fatal errors through analyzing error logs;
Build pages with page builders like Elementor, Beaver Builder, WP Bakery, Avada, etc;
Speed optimizations;
Malware removals;
Audit existing projects and look for any issues that should be addressed;
Work with the support lead to improve documentation & general processes;
Run Unix commands for migrations / troubleshooting;
Perform weekly plugin / theme / WP core updates and run visual tests;
Create / maintain plugins & themes;

Requirements

Strong understanding of WordPress and its architecture
Excellent problem-solving skills
Excellent written and verbal communication skills [in English]
Ability to work well under pressure and handle multiple tasks simultaneously (you'll be handling a lot of business-critical issues on a daily-basis)
Strong attention to detail

Preferred Qualifications:

PHP
WordPress
CSS/JS/HTML
Page Builders (WP Bakery, Beaver Builder, Elementor, Avada)
Troubleshooting & log analysis (!important)
Advanced WordPress theme & plugin editing
WordPress actions & filters
Advanced jQuery
a good understanding of Web services, REST and RPC APIs
proficiency with code versioning tools, such as Git
built plugins & themes in the past
Fluent in written English

Dockstr is looking for an ambitious SENIOR FULL-STACK REMOTE DEVELOPER professional with an entrepreneurial spirit. Someone excited for a new challenge where you would have the space to grow and make an impact. You should be comfortable operating in an international and fast paced environment where you can become a valuable member of our team.

This is for a PART-TIME position initially but it may evolved over time to a full time position.

RESPONSIBILITIES:
- Lead a number of product development areas;
- Contribute to taking our existing technical solutions to the next level;
- Take a leading role in the area of UX, UI and front-end development of our solutions;
- When it comes to UX/UI, you will help us to bring together exceptional design, creativity and usability;
- Play a key role in building our tech team for the future and setting the team culture to deliver products that exceed expectations.

OUR STACK:
- Frontend: JS, React, Apollo, GraphQL, SASS, Material UI
- Server: Ruby, Ruby on Rails, Elasticsearch, Redis, AWS S3
- Tools and services: Github, Slack

WE ARE LOOKING FOR AN ENGINEER WITH:
- 5-7 years of experience in designing, building Ruby on Rails applications;
- Proﬁciency in front-end and back-end development;
- Track-record of continuous integration and delivery;
- Familiarity with Heroku and Postgres;
- Fluency in English;
- Creative, ﬂexible, and meticulous working style.

SET-UP:
- Remote;
- Part-time - between 40 to 80 hours a month initially.

The potential for you to grow with us and to inﬂuence our direction is not insignificant. So if you’re a confident developer, wondering where you could achieve maximum impact, why not consider working with one of the best early-stage startups in Scandinavia and put your skills/experience into action.

If you think your proﬁle, capabilities and ambition match our plans then ping us and let’s talk!
